      "summary": "Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez has called an extraordinary meeting of the National Security Council for Tuesday to analyze the situation in Ceuta, nearly a month after a mass migrant crossing into the autonomous city. The council will address the territorial integrity concerns raised by the influx of migrants who entered Ceuta from Morocco.",
      "takeaway": "Spain's delayed institutional response to the Ceuta crisis indicates the government is still developing its strategy for managing the border and migrant pressure.",
      "why_it_matters": "The Spanish government's convening of the National Security Council signals an acknowledgment that the mass migrant assault on Ceuta nearly a month prior demands a formal security response, though the articles provide no specifics about what decisions will be made or implemented."
